==Russian==

===Etymology===
See {{m|ru|при}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|при-}}
* {{ru-IPA|при́-}} {{q|when stressed}}

===Prefix===
{{head|ru|prefix|cat2=verbal prefixes}}

# {{lb|ru|used with verbs}} [[arrival]]
#: {{prefex|ru|-йти́|t1=to [[go]]|прийти́|t2=to [[come]]}}
#: {{prefex|ru|лете́ть|t1=to [[fly]]|прилете́ть|t2=to [[arrive]] by [[plane]]}}
# {{lb|ru|used with verbs}} [[attachment]], [[on]]
#: {{prefex|ru|шить|t1=to [[sew]]|приши́ть|t2=to [[sew]] [[on]]}}
#: {{prefex|ru|винти́ть|t1=to [[screw]]|привинти́ть|t2=to [[screw]] [[on]], to [[attach]] by [[screw]]ing}}
#: {{prefex|ru|крути́ть|t1=to [[twist]], to [[spin]]|прикрути́ть|t2=to [[spin]] [[on]], to [[attach]] by [[spin]]ning; to [[screw]] [[in]]}}
# {{lb|ru|used with verbs}} [[add]]ing to
#: {{prefex|ru|писа́ть|t1=to [[write]]|приписа́ть|t2=to [[add]] in [[writing]]}}
#: {{prefex|ru|купи́ть|t1=to [[buy]]|прикупи́ть|t2=to [[buy]] some [[more]]}}
#: {{prefex|ru|-ба́вить|приба́вить|t2=to [[add]]}}
# {{lb|ru|used with verbs}} [[slightly]], [[partially]]
#: {{prefex|ru|отвори́ть|t1=to [[open]]|приотвори́ть|t2=to [[open]] [[slightly]]}}
#: {{prefex|ru|спусти́ть|t1=to [[lower]]|приспусти́ть|t2=to [[lower]] [[partially]]}}
# {{lb|ru|place names}} [[by]], [[near]], [[next to]]
#: {{prefex|ru|Карпа́ты|t1=[[Carpathians]]|-ье|Прикарпа́тье|t3=[[Prykarpattia]], [[Circumcarpathia]]|lit3=near the Carpathian Mountains}}
#: {{prefex|ru|Днестр|t1=[[Dniester]] {{q|river}}|-о́вый|-ье|Приднестро́вье|t4=[[Transnistria]]|lit4=next to the Dniester River}}
#: {{prefex|ru|мо́ре|t1=[[sea]]|-ский|край|t3=[[krai]], [[territory]]|Примо́рский край|t4=[[Primorsky Krai]]|lit4=seaside territory}}
#: {{prefex|ru|Днепр|t1=[[Dnieper]] {{q|river}}|-о́вский|Приднепро́вский|lit3=near the [[Dnieper]]}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[Приднепро́вская ни́зменность]]|[[Dnieper Lowland]]|lit=lowland by the Dnieper River}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[Приднепро́вская желе́зная доро́га]]|[[Near-Dnipro Railway]]}}

====Usage notes====
* The stressed variant is found in the following situations:
*# the past participle of verbs with a one-syllable root ending in {{lang|ru|-ать}} and {{lang|ru|-нуть}}: e.g. {{m|ru|при́знанный}} from {{m|ru|призна́ть}}, {{m|ru|при́гнанный}} from {{m|ru|пригна́ть}}, {{m|ru|при́гнутый}} from {{m|ru|пригну́ть}};
*# the past tense of some verbs with a one-syllable root: e.g. {{m|ru|[[приме́рь]]}} from {{m|ru|примерить||to [[try]] on {{q|low colloquial}}}};
*# some deverbal and other derived nouns: e.g. {{m|ru|при́вязь||[[leash]]}} from {{m|ru|привяза́ть||to [[tie]] (to)}}, {{m|ru|при́быль||[[profit]]}} from {{m|ru|прибы́ть||to [[increase]]}}, {{m|ru|при́город||[[suburb]]}} from {{m|ru|го́род||[[city]]}}, {{m|ru|при́иск||[[mine]]}} from {{m|ru|прииска́ть||to [[find]] {{q|colloquial}}}}, {{m|ru|при́сказка||[[prelude]]}} from {{m|ru|ска́зка||[[tale]]}}, {{m|ru|при́хоть||[[whim]]}} from {{m|ru|хоте́ть||to [[want]]}}.

====Derived terms====
{{prefixsee|ru}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ru|при}}

